    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0435" n="1169" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1169"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-16"><hi rendition="#italic">July 16,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Summoned to-day by minister of state, who told me confidentially that after the
                    council of to-morrow he would be able to answer officially my note of June 18,
                    demanding payment of Mora indemnity, that the council yesterday resolved to
                    offer to satisfy said demand by payment of the principal in three installments
                    at the times indicated in your conversation with Dupuy of the 21st June. While
                    clearly expressing his expectation to pay principal only, he declined to
                    intimate whether he proposed to tender gold or depreciated Spanish currency.
                    What shall I say on that point?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taylor.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
